      "mergeID": "6a8d6d7112ade8af1882ddec",
      "mergedPostDetails": "It would be a great feature, especially because all the blush effects on the avatars just looks bad without the transparency (who don't enable the shaders on the avatars), so at least, we could just disable the blush effect by this parameter if the shaders are turned off. Also, even if we try to use the Poiyomi's shader and set the fallback shader to transparent, it does absolutely nothing.\n\nAlso it could provide more performance benefits too, since it would allow the avatar creators to both utilize the UV tile discard and the usage of blendshape driven toggles too, so the creators could make both animation clips for hiding the object by the UV discard system or by a blendshape if the player turned off the shaders on the avatars.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "provide `IsShadersEnabled` parameter as a built-in parameter.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64dfba6b8e02e5093572fc04",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would go with the parameter name `IsUsingFallbackShaders` instead, but it would essentially work the same way.\n\nSuch a parameter is also helpful for dealing with Poiyomi's World AO Blocker feature where the eyes of certain avatars, such as the Jinxed Dog, will look bizarre if fallback shaders are used because the extra geometry that Poiyomi usually hides gets rendered by the fallback.\n\nWith this parameter, we can use a shape key to pull the World AO Blocker geometry into the head so the eyes look more normal when fallback shaders are in use.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
